    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d698">

                <pb facs="0611" n="599" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg599"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.51/1782: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-03-19T14:00:00-03:00">March 19, 1940—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>117. Department’s 76, March 18, 2 p.m. Aranha says that he is willing for the
                    Brazilian Government to promise to “advise bondholders in advance of purchases,
                    et cetera, et cetera” as set out in the Council’s inquiry and he feels
                    reasonably sure the Minister of Finance will agree. Souza Costa is in Pocos de
                    Caldas and Aranha will go there on Saturday, discuss the matter with him and
                    send me a reply to the question in writing.<anchor n="25a" xml:id="d698-f1"
                    /></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d698-f1" n="25a" xml:id="d698-f1-content">
                <p>Affirmative reply in writing contained in telegram No. 126, March 25, 1940, 5
                    p.m., from Rio de Janeiro; not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
